{
  "title": "Golden Line: Toward What Matters",
  "description": "<p>A directional instrument for recording long-horizon aspirations and observable movement toward them. It returns one of four directional readings per aspiration against a versioned registry and deliberately computes no aggregate: there is no virtue score, and NOT_OBSERVED means no valid entry was admitted rather than that nobody looked.</p><p><strong>Subtitle:</strong> An Aspirational Thread for Long-Horizon Work</p><p>Code is MIT licensed; prose and figures are CC BY 4.0. See LICENSE in the repository.</p>",
